Wait, I need to reconsider this. Looking at the file changes again - only TypeScript/React files are being modified (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`). There are no build artifacts, dependency directories, or temporary files in the change list. According to rule #6, if the change list contains only source or config files and no build artifacts, dependencies, or temp files, I should output an empty .gitignore.

Since only `.tsx` files are being modified, which are source code files, no additional ignores are needed beyond what might already be appropriate for a Next.js/React project.

